---
import Page from "@layouts/Page.astro";
import { CONTACT_LANGUAGES } from "@lib/legal";
import { LEGAL } from "@lib/legal-env";

const mailto = `mailto:${LEGAL.email}`;
---

<Page
	title="Terms of use"
	description="The rules for using Factorio Expo: the licence you grant for uploads, what may not be uploaded, the fair use policy, takedowns and moderation."
>
	<h1>Terms of use</h1>
	<p>
		<small>Last updated: 6 November 2026</small>
	</p>
	<p>
		Factorio Expo is a free, non-commercial fan site run by {LEGAL.name}. By uploading,
		commenting or creating an account you agree to these terms. Browsing needs no account and no
		agreement beyond the law. How personal data is handled is in the{" "}
		<a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
	<p>
		One address for everything: questions, takedown requests, reports of illegal content,
		security issues and requests from authorities: <a href={mailto}>{LEGAL.email}</a>. It is the
		single point of contact for users and authorities under Articles 11 and 12 of the Digital
		Services Act, answered by a person in {CONTACT_LANGUAGES.join(" or ")}.
	</p>

	<h2 id="age">Age</h2>
	<p>You must be at least 16 years old to upload, comment or create an account.</p>

	<h2 id="licence">Your uploads and the licence you grant</h2>
	<p>
		What you upload stays yours: the exchange string, its title, description and tags, and your
		comments. You grant the operator of Factorio Expo a free, non-exclusive, worldwide licence
		to:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			store the exact string you uploaded and its decoded contents, and keep every revision;
		</li>
		<li>
			render previews with the game, analyse it (contents, power, production rates, platform
			stats), and render and analyse it again, for example with a newer game version;
		</li>
		<li>
			show and serve all of that to visitors, including the string to copy into the game and
			the preview images, as far as the visibility you chose allows (a private entry is shown
			to you only);
		</li>
		<li>index it for the site's search and list it on the site's pages.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		The licence ends when the entry or comment is deleted. What is left is erased as the{" "}
		<a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> describes, and backups expire within 30 days. A
		deleted comment leaves an empty placeholder so the thread's numbering stays intact.
	</p>
	<p>
		Sharing blueprints is the point of the site: anyone may copy a public or unlisted entry's
		string and use it in their own game. These terms grant nothing beyond that; to republish
		someone's blueprint elsewhere, ask its author.
	</p>
	<p>
		You may only upload what you have the right to share: your own work, or someone else's with
		their permission. An anonymous entry has no owner; whoever holds its edit link can change or
		delete it, so keep the link private. A lost edit link cannot be recovered.
	</p>

	<h2 id="not-allowed">What may not be uploaded</h2>
	<p>
		These rules cover everything you put on the site: exchange strings, the labels, descriptions
		and pixel art inside them, entry titles, descriptions, tags, comments and usernames.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Anything illegal, or that links to illegal content.</li>
		<li>Someone else's work without their permission.</li>
		<li>
			Hate, harassment, threats, sexual content, graphic violence, or anything targeting a
			person or group.
		</li>
		<li>Other people's personal data.</li>
		<li>Spam, advertising, and titles, descriptions or tags that misrepresent the entry.</li>
		<li>
			Strings crafted to harm the site, its renderer or players' games. Found a weakness?
			Write to <a href={mailto}>{LEGAL.email}</a> instead (see{" "}
			<a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a>).
		</li>
		<li>Usernames that impersonate someone else, staff, or Wube Software.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="fair-use">Fair use policy</h2>
	<p>
		Every preview is rendered by one shared copy of Factorio, so everyone waits in the same
		queue. To keep it fair:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Rate limits.</strong> Uploads, previews, revisions, reports, comments and
			sign-ins are limited per address and per account.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>A cap on waiting renders.</strong> Each uploader (an account, or an address when
			not signed in) may only have a limited number of blueprints waiting to render. An upload
			that would go over it is refused as a whole with "too many blueprints waiting to
			render"; try again once some have finished.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Order.</strong> One uploader's blueprints are spaced out, so a big book shares
			the renderer with everyone else's work instead of blocking it. Signed-in uploads start
			sooner than anonymous ones, and re-rendering an old preview waits a little longer. Quick
			previews are not delayed.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Bot check.</strong> Uploads, previews, revisions and reports made without
			signing in pass a Cloudflare Turnstile check.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Automation.</strong> Uploading by script or bot, mass imports and scraping need
			a signed-in account and permission first: ask at <a href={mailto}>{LEGAL.email}</a>.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>No working around it.</strong> Do not use several accounts or addresses to get
			past a limit or a ban.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		The exact limits change with the load and are not published. Abuse can lead to tighter
		limits, removed entries and a ban.
	</p>

	<h2 id="moderation">Moderation</h2>
	<p>
		Anyone can report an entry with its flag button, and signed-in users can report comments.
		Every report is reviewed by a person; reports never hide anything automatically, however
		many there are. The site makes no automated moderation decisions: the only automated checks
		are the upload format and size limits, the rate limits and the bot check above.
	</p>
	<p>When content breaks these terms or the law, staff may, depending on how serious it is:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>delete an entry, or remove a comment (it stays as "Removed by staff");</li>
		<li>
			ban an account from uploading, commenting or reporting, for a time or permanently, and
			block the addresses it used for a few hours;
		</li>
		<li>delete an account.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		The reason for every decision is recorded. The site has no email address for you, so it
		cannot always tell you itself; ask at <a href={mailto}>{LEGAL.email}</a> and you get the
		reason. To object to a decision, write to the same address saying which entry, comment or
		account it is about and why the decision is wrong. A person who did not make the decision
		reviews it where possible, and you get an answer.
	</p>

	<h2 id="takedown">Takedown requests and illegal content</h2>
	<p>
		If an entry is your work posted without your permission, report it with its flag button,
		choose "Someone else's work, posted without permission" and link to your original (a post,
		video or save). For anything else illegal, or if you prefer email, write to{" "}
		<a href={mailto}>{LEGAL.email}</a> with:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>the link to each entry, blueprint or comment (for example /e/abc123def456);</li>
		<li>why it is illegal or which of your rights it infringes;</li>
		<li>your name and email address;</li>
		<li>
			a statement that you believe in good faith that the information is accurate and
			complete.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Each notice is handled promptly by a person. If you gave an email address you get a receipt
		and the decision. The uploader can object as described under moderation above. Notices that
		are knowingly false can lead to a ban from reporting.
	</p>

	<h2 id="accounts">Accounts</h2>
	<p>
		An account is for one person. Keep your sign-in methods safe: whoever can sign in to them
		can act as you. You can delete your account at any time on your{" "}
		<a href="/account">account page</a>; what happens then is in the{" "}
		<a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="no-warranty">No warranty</h2>
	<p>
		Factorio Expo is free and provided as it is. Previews, analysis and production rates come
		from the game but can still be wrong or missing. The site may change, pause or end features
		or the whole service, entries expire when their uploader chose so, and entries may be
		removed. Keep your own copy of every string you care about.
	</p>
	<p>
		The operator is liable only for intent and gross negligence. This does not limit liability
		for injury to life, body or health, or where the law does not allow a limit.
	</p>

	<h2 id="factorio">Factorio</h2>
	<p>
		Factorio Expo is not affiliated with or endorsed by Wube Software. The game's graphics,
		icons and data shown on the site belong to Wube Software (
		<a href="/about#unofficial">more</a>).
	</p>

	<h2 id="changes">Changes and applicable law</h2>
	<p>
		These terms change when the site does; the date above shows the latest version, and a change
		that affects you is announced on the site first. Personal data is handled under the GDPR
		(see the <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>). If you are a consumer, the mandatory
		consumer protection of the country you live in applies.
	</p>
</Page>
